The other charged twenty-seven cents.

3
00:00:05,230 --> 00:00:07,520
Meet Opus 5 and Opus 5.5.

4
00:00:07,660 --> 00:00:09,350
They work, and I supervise.

5
00:00:09,540 --> 00:00:12,270
Each got one try at the same real dashboard job.

6
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:15,240
Opus 5.5 was done in fifty-three seconds.

7
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:17,850
The older model took two hundred and sixty-five.

8
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:20,040
I can't find my remote that fast.

9
00:00:20,230 --> 00:00:22,460
Yet both passed all eighteen hidden tests.

10
00:00:22,590 --> 00:00:24,910
The new one took five steps, not thirty-one.

11
00:00:24,990 --> 00:00:27,250
Fewer steps mean a smaller API bill.

12
00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:29,410
But it never checked its page in a browser.

13
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:33,190
It skipped checking its own work. I've never felt so seen.

14
00:00:33,380 --> 00:00:35,330
The full test is in the long video.

15
00:00:35,470 --> 00:00:37,640
So yes, I'm upgrading, because...
